# Family preview parity

When adding or changing a **parent portal**, **apply dashboard**, or **enrollment checklist** feature:

1. **Find the live route** under `src/app/school/[slug]/...`
2. **Find or add the matching preview route** under `src/app/admin/(preview)/preview/[slug]/family/[familyId]/...`
3. **Reuse the same client component** — do not fork UI or fall through to Coming Soon when live has a real implementation
4. **Load the same server data** scoped to the previewed family (`family-preview-access.ts` helpers + admin client where auth differs)
5. **Visual parity**: show the same sections/forms/buttons as live; use `previewMode` / `readOnly` to **disable interactions**, not to hide UI
6. **Verify** from `/admin/organizations` → submission Preview → compare with live parent/apply view

## Preview route map

| Live | Family preview |
|------|----------------|
| `/school/{slug}/apply` | `/admin/preview/{slug}/family/{familyId}` |
| `/school/{slug}/apply/{appId}` | `.../apply/{appId}` |
| `/school/{slug}/apply/{appId}/enrollment` | `.../apply/{appId}/enrollment` |
| `/school/{slug}/parent/{feature}` | `.../parent/{feature}` |

## Common pitfalls

- Preview route missing a `feature === "..."` branch that live parent route has
- Client fetches parent-portal APIs authenticated as the logged-in admin — load data server-side for preview instead
- Gating UI on `isLive` or `previewMode` when only actions should be blocked (e.g. combined payment, join-request forms)
